questions.questionText:
An electron in the Coulomb field of a proton is in the following state of coherent superposition of orthonormal states 𝜓_{𝑛𝑙𝑚}

Ψ = 1 3 𝜓_{100} + 1 \sqrt 3 𝜓_{210} - \sqrt 5 3 𝜓_{320}

Let 𝐸_{1}, 𝐸_{2}, and 𝐸_{3} represent the first three energy levels of the system. A sequence of measurements is done on the same system at different times. Energy is measured first at time 𝑡_{1} and the outcome is 𝐸_{2}. Then total angular momentum is measured at time 𝑡_{2} > 𝑡_{1} and finally energy is measured again at 𝑡_{3} > 𝑡_{2}. The probability of finding the system in a state with energy 𝐸_{2} after the final measurement is 𝑃/9. The value of 𝑃 is _____ (in integer).

